riangle ABE \\):**\n   - The area of a triangle is given by \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} \\).\n   - The base \\( \\overline{AD} \\) is 18.\n   - The height from \\( B \\) to \\( \\overline{AD} \\) is the y-coordinate of \\( B \\), which is 24.\n   - Therefore, the area of \\( \\triangle ABE \\) is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{1}{2} \\times 18 \\times 24 = 216\n     \\]\n   - The correct option is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
